Title: Iconify on AROS, and reply to Workbench messages
Repository: SDL 3.4.12 with contrib SDL3-3.4.12-aros.diff (contrib 142b3ff4)
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-sdl project
Problem: AROS_CheckWBEvents never replied to AppMessages; Workbench waits for the reply while holding its lock, so dropping files on a window froze the system (the same bug was fixed in the SDL2 port in deadwood2/contrib abdd0267). The iconify gadget "hid" windows through window opacity, which does nothing on AROS, and created an AppIcon only when the program had its own icon or ENVARC:Sys/def_SDL existed: the window stayed and no icon appeared.
Change: Reply to every AppMessage after handling it. On AROS, iconify hides the windows with HideWindow and sends SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MINIMIZED, only when the AppIcon was added; the AppIcon brings them back with ShowWindow and SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESTORED. Programs without an icon iconify to the default tool icon.
Scope: AROS (src/video/aros)
Upstream: https://github.com/aros-development-team/contrib/pull/92 (open, submitted 2026-11-16)
Verification: Built for mainline x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK 20261110); pool v1-1 (nightly 20261113), 2026-11-16: the iconify gadget hides the self-test window, a default tool AppIcon appears, a double-click on it brings the window back (SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MINIMIZED 521 and RESTORED 523 logged); a PNG icon dropped from a Wanderer drawer onto a LibreSprite window opens the file, Workbench keeps running
Contrib branch: tomaszstaniak/contrib sdl3-iconify-appmessage-reply 5002e9e6, on contrib master 142b3ff4; built in-tree and checked before/after 2026-11-16 (tests/aros/sdl3-contrib-check.c); PR not opened yet
Removal: when contrib has an equivalent change
---
diff -ru a/src/video/aros/SDL_arosevents.c b/src/video/aros/SDL_arosevents.c
--- a/src/video/aros/SDL_arosevents.c	2026-11-16 13:55:05
+++ b/src/video/aros/SDL_arosevents.c	2026-11-16 13:55:05
@@ -835,6 +835,9 @@
 				break;
 		}
 
+		/* Workbench waits for the reply while it holds its lock: without it a
+		   drop on the window (or a double-click on the AppIcon) froze it. */
+		ReplyMsg(&msg->am_Message);
 	}
 }
 
diff -ru a/src/video/aros/SDL_arosvideo.c b/src/video/aros/SDL_arosvideo.c
--- a/src/video/aros/SDL_arosvideo.c	2026-11-16 13:55:05
+++ b/src/video/aros/SDL_arosvideo.c	2026-11-16 13:55:05
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 #include "../SDL_sysvideo.h"
 #include "../SDL_pixels_c.h"
+#include "../../events/SDL_events_c.h"
 
 #include "SDL_arosclipboard.h"
 
@@ -145,6 +146,18 @@
 
 	if (with_app_icon && data->AppIcon)
 		data->AppIconRef = AddAppIconA(0, 0, FilePart(data->FullAppName), &data->WBPort, 0, data->AppIcon, NULL);
+
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+	/* Window opacity does nothing on AROS: hide the windows instead, but only
+	   when the AppIcon is there to bring them back. */
+	if (with_app_icon && data->AppIconRef) {
+		ForeachNode(&data->windowlist, wd)
+		{
+			if (wd->win && HideWindow(wd->win))
+				SDL_SendWindowEvent(wd->window, SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MINIMIZED, 0, 0);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 }
 
 void
@@ -169,6 +182,10 @@
     {
         struct Window *win = wd->win;
         if (win) {
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+            if (ShowWindow(win, WINDOW_FRONTMOST))
+                SDL_SendWindowEvent(wd->window, SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESTORED, 0, 0);
+#endif
             AROS_SetWindowOpacity(_this, wd->window, 1.0);
             AROS_WindowToFront(win);
         }
@@ -384,6 +401,11 @@
 
 			if (data->AppIcon == NULL)
 				data->AppIcon = GetDiskObject((STRPTR)"ENVARC:Sys/def_SDL");
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+			/* A program without its own icon still gets one to iconify to. */
+			if (data->AppIcon == NULL)
+				data->AppIcon = GetDefDiskObject(WBTOOL);
+#endif
 
 			if (data->AppIcon) {
 				data->AppIcon->do_CurrentX = NO_ICON_POSITION;
